      },
      "worked": "A rectangle with sides of 2 parts and 3 parts contains 6 equal squares, each with side length 1 part.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Number of squares}&=2\\times3=6\\\\\\text{Area of one square}&=54\\div6=9\\text{ cm}^2\\\\\\text{Length of one part}&=\\sqrt{9}=3\\text{ cm}\\\\\\text{Length}&=2\\times3=6\\text{ cm}\\\\\\text{Width}&=3\\times3=9\\text{ cm}\\\\\\text{Perimeter}&=2(6+9)\\\\\\text{Perimeter}&=30\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
